["math" "-\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{6}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{(s-4)^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340844" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340844" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340844" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340844" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={{field-4}},\\,s>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =-4({s}^{2}+16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{(s)^{′}\\cdot ({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot {(({s}^{2}+16)^{2})}^{′}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot 2({s}^{2}+16)\\cdot 2s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-4{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+16)}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{{s}^{2}+16-4{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{16-3{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the quotient rule to find ${F}^{″}(s).$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}={F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fc6737efff481bdca94dbf64cdeca031f12322707bd827a273b1cc87496bbb3"} {"question" "q-340850" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93fe219c3c913a6acc3484ed6a171f29d4cb12ef105138719cc6d8d0c09d379d"} {"question" "q-340850" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{F}^{″}(s)"] ["math" "-{s}^{2}{F}^{′}(s)"] ["math" "-{s}^{2}{F}^{″}(s)"] ["math" "{F}^{″}(s)"] ["math" "{s}^{2}{F}^{″}(s)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074297/state